{:edb/db-before-t 1823 :edb/db-after-t 1824 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535136 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:45:29.143Z" 13194139535136 true] [17592186198287 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333147 13194139535136 true] [17592186198287 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333167 13194139535136 true] [17592186198297 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333154 13194139535136 true] [17592186198874 1017 #edb/ref 17592186197479 13194139535136 false] [17592186198874 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333161 13194139535136 true] [17592186198874 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535136 true] [17592186198874 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T$, where $T$ is defined as\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u^{2} + v^{2} \\\\ uv\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535136 false] [17592186198874 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186198874 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=uv.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2v \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot u-2v\\cdot v \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {v}^{2} & ={u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation ${v}^{2}={u}^{2}$ defines a pair of intersecting lines $v=u$ and $v=-u$ in the $uv$-plane." 13194139535136 true] [17592186198930 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535136 true] [17592186198930 1100 "Consider the transformation $T: (u, v) → (x(u, v), y(u, v))$. The inverse transformation $T^{-1}(x, y) → (u(x, y), v(x, y))$ is given by\n\n$T^{-1}: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2x + 3y \\\\ 2x + y\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T$." 13194139535136 false] [17592186198930 1100 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x+3y \\\\ 2x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186198930 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $u(x,y)=2x+3y$ and $v(x,y)=2x+y.$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333147 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333148 13194139535136 true] [17592186333147 1089 "q-160465" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333147 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535136 true] [17592186333147 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ {u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333147 1113 #uuid "6940edb0-4ff9-5079-afa0-d099bcae85dd" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333147 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={e}^{u+v}$ and $y(u,v)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={e}^{u+v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ 2u & 2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot 2v-{e}^{u+v}\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =2{e}^{u+v}(v-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 2{e}^{u+v}(v-u) & =0 \\\\ v-u & =0 \\\\ u & =v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u=v$ defines a line in the $uv$-plane." 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333149 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333150 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333151 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333152 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333153 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1041 "selection" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333153 13194139535136 true] [17592186333148 1110 #uuid "bd0aeab8-1cb7-5313-abf6-d718134ac07e" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333149 1034 "The critical points lie on the line $u=-2v.$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535136 true] [17592186333149 1111 #uuid "d2433591-06e6-5786-ae94-916b90ab9a2c" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333150 1034 "The critical points lie on the line $v=-2u.$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535136 true] [17592186333150 1111 #uuid "f6bc6899-080a-5546-a994-4f50159fd979" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333151 1034 "The critical points lie on the line $v=2u.$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535136 true] [17592186333151 1111 #uuid "f6e5e006-1b27-547f-89f1-e0bf72d6c425" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333152 1034 "The critical points lie on the line $u=-v.$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535136 true] [17592186333152 1111 #uuid "b6aa4e1c-d9ca-5cb6-a1f0-9dcc0dc868d7" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333153 1034 "The critical points lie on the line $u=v.$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535136 true] [17592186333153 1111 #uuid "473e9830-80c3-5dcf-89d4-ac135579a3e3" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333154 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333155 13194139535136 true] [17592186333154 1089 "q-160582" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333154 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535136 true] [17592186333154 1100 "Consider all non-critical points of the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{y}{x}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333154 1113 #uuid "f5c689ee-f9f4-5966-afaa-66a344e58af4" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333154 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $u(x,y)={e}^{xy}$ and $v(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}.$ \n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =y{e}^{xy} & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =x{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy} \\\\ -\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}-x{e}^{xy}\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y{e}^{xy}}{x} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =2uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2uv}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333156 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333157 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333158 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333159 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333160 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1041 "selection" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333156 13194139535136 true] [17592186333155 1110 #uuid "a0b1f2e3-10b8-56e9-909f-37dcc42ae1b0" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333156 1034 "\\frac{1}{2uv}" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535136 true] [17592186333156 1111 #uuid "bba65baa-7359-5bd4-b666-c85b5debabca" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333157 1034 "-\\frac{v}{u}" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535136 true] [17592186333157 1111 #uuid "704abbbd-e91c-51c1-bed8-4e24c6889c90" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333158 1034 "\\frac{u}{v}" 13194139535136 true] [17592186333158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535136 true] [17592186333158 1111 #uuid "aa7b